=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: host_1_1_1_1
diagnosis_text:
The fault is a misconfigured default gateway on host_1_1_1_1. The host has
its default route set to 10.1.1.254 (`default via 10.1.1.254 dev eth0`),
but no device in the 10.1.1.0/24 subnet holds that address. The actual
Layer-3 gateway for the pod-1 LAN is switch_dist_1_1, whose bridge
interface br0 is assigned 10.1.1.1/24. Because 10.1.1.254 is phantom,
every ARP request the host sends for its gateway goes unanswered; the
kernel returns "Destination Host Unreachable" for all off-subnet traffic
and the host is effectively black-holed beyond its own /24.

The symptom pattern matches exactly: pinging 10.1.1.1 works because that
address IS reachable via direct on-link ARP (no default route needed);
pinging any off-subnet target (10.2.1.x, 10.200.0.x, etc.) fails because
the host cannot forward those packets without a live gateway. host_2_1_1_1
is unaffected because its distribution switch (switch_dist_2_1) is
configured consistently with that host's gateway setting.

Root cause: host_1_1_1_1's default gateway is statically configured as
10.1.1.254 instead of the correct address 10.1.1.1.

Corrective fix: On host_1_1_1_1, replace the default route:
  ip route del default
  ip route add default via 10.1.1.1 dev eth0
Then update the persistent startup configuration (e.g., /etc/network/
interfaces or the Kathara startup script) to set `gateway 10.1.1.1` so
the correct gateway survives a container restart.
=== END ===
